			"date": "2023-01-30T20:13:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@sil\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>sil</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jaffathecake\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jaffathecake</span></a></span> well \"content\" is probably a meaningless word but typically in the context of the web i meant \"hypertext\" and even if you extend the idea to embedded media, figma design files are not really \"web\" in any meaningful way (unless you create a sharing link). you could have it all native and nothing would change</p><p>as for websites that fetch and manipulate data while performing actions, i think those cease to be websites. maybe hybrid website/webapp, but not purely a site.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
