			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@sil\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>sil</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jaffathecake\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jaffathecake</span></a></span> I don't see it exactly as a dichotomy. I think apps can do everything sites can or should do, but something cataloged as an \"app\" is generally more interactive, whereas \"sites\" tend to be more \"read-only\"</p>",
