			},
			"date": "2023-01-31T12:25:09.973Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a class=\"u-url mention\" href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a class=\"u-url mention\" href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jaffathecake\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jaffathecake</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a class=\"u-url mention\" href=\"https://paquita.masto.host/@juandjara\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>juandjara</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a class=\"u-url mention\" href=\"https://mastodon.social/@sil\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>sil</span></a></span> I would say if an “web address” can be meaningfully preserved as a PDF, it’s a <em>site</em>, otherwise an <em>app</em>.</p><p>I find that distinction meaningful, most other ways if drawing a line feel like purity policing. (Which I am sometimes guilty of, myself.)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
