		{
			"id": "109784269895005251",
			"parentId": "109783839376180689",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109784269895005251",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-31T14:23:36.706Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fedi.gerwitz.com/@hans/\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>hans</span></a></span> sorry to 5 whys you but I think the question I’d like an answer to is: meaningful how? for what? I think there is more gold in those answers</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109785051570344686",
			"parentId": "109784269895005251",
			"url": "https://social.gerwitz.com/objects/8e075057-fa93-485a-a57f-5694d11725bb",
			"author": {
				"name": "Hans Gerwitz",
				"url": "https://fedi.gerwitz.com/@hans/",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/416/536/212/833/756/original/e61193cab5cb11c1.webp"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-31T17:42:22.547Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a class=\"u-url mention\" href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> no worries!</p><p>Meaningful because a “site” is meant for information sharing across both space and time. It’s made of URLs that represent long-lived information resources meant to be linked to. It’s the WEB, FFS.</p><p>Apps are pieces of software that use www infrastructure for deployment. Which is a cool hack but should not be confused for being a member of the web-of-URLs.</p><p>They may coexist on a domain, mind you. But usually don’t.</p><p>(I am growing to think ActivityPub heralds a third category, of conversational “social” apps.)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		}
	],
